Nihilumbra is very enjoyable 2D platformer where you use various elemental themed colours/powers to "draw" said colours onto walls, floors and ceilings to slide, jump, and stick your way over and around obstacles and enemies. The overall story is slightly dark and focuses on you, a small spawn of the "Void", trying to escape from where you were born and find a reason to live in these strange, new (to you) worlds.
Overall a fun game I got off of Humble Bundle that took me almost 2 hours to beat the story. The game also features a challenge mode after beating the main story which I plan to get into at a later date. Glad I played it.
Edit: it actually took me a little over 3 hours to beat the main story because I was attempting to get the "Pacifist" achievement on my first playthrough. Still ended up not getting it. ; _ ;

